gallons

00:14:21.660 --> 00:14:24.900
show to the

00:14:24.900 --> 00:14:27.000
that they are received

00:14:27.000 --> 00:14:29.080
in a proper way.

00:14:29.260 --> 00:14:30.160
You know? Right?

00:14:31.740 --> 00:14:33.120
Now, one thing we learn

00:14:33.120 --> 00:14:35.060
about him is he promises

00:14:35.060 --> 00:14:37.000
a little, he does a lot. But there's

00:14:37.000 --> 00:14:39.260
another thing we should remember

00:14:39.260 --> 00:14:40.500
about us also.

00:14:40.500 --> 00:14:47.500
Ahnasat al-Arhim. Ahnasat al-Arhim to invite guests was considered as one of the greatest musbahs.

00:14:47.500 --> 00:14:53.500
Especially somebody comes from the outside and so on. This was a particular among the Sefardim, that was a great musbah.

00:14:53.500 --> 00:15:00.500
And I believe that no matter how modern we are, still we should remember this musbah.

00:15:00.500 --> 00:15:06.500
It's an important musbah because everybody, you know, in other words, socialize among people.

00:15:06.500 --> 00:15:08.600
because people

00:15:08.600 --> 00:15:11.100
become more humane

00:15:11.100 --> 00:15:12.440
through human character.

00:15:12.860 --> 00:15:14.960
You invite people, and this is very important,

00:15:15.120 --> 00:15:16.940
akharsat or him, especially

00:15:16.940 --> 00:15:18.620
in the case that Abraham did it

00:15:18.620 --> 00:15:20.680
to somebody who was a stranger.

00:15:20.760 --> 00:15:22.460
This is a great muslim, akharsat or him.

00:15:22.460 --> 00:15:22.880
Alright?

00:15:24.160 --> 00:15:26.340
Rabbi, does this imply that he did this every time

00:15:26.340 --> 00:15:27.880
a stranger came past his table?

00:15:28.660 --> 00:15:30.240
Yeah. Abraham, this is the

00:15:30.240 --> 00:15:31.520
muslim, akharsat or him.

00:15:32.660 --> 00:15:34.060
Hospitality. He used to stand,

00:15:34.180 --> 00:15:35.520
the rabbi says he used to stand up.

00:15:35.520 --> 00:15:36.740
And the crossroads.

00:15:37.380 --> 00:15:39.460
And anybody who is passing by,

00:15:39.680 --> 00:15:40.060
come down.

00:15:40.100 --> 00:15:40.520
By the way,

00:15:40.600 --> 00:15:41.840
this was the custom among us.

00:15:41.920 --> 00:15:43.180
I remember many years ago

00:15:43.180 --> 00:15:44.400
when I was a child,

00:15:44.840 --> 00:15:46.240
if a stranger would come to the synagogue,

00:15:46.720 --> 00:15:47.700
stranger comes to the synagogue,

00:15:47.860 --> 00:15:49.020
immediately everybody fighting

00:15:49.020 --> 00:15:50.060
who is going to invite him to the home.

00:15:50.200 --> 00:15:51.440
This is what everybody would invite.

00:15:51.560 --> 00:15:52.720
What you see as a great spouse,

00:15:52.880 --> 00:15:53.720
what you see as a great privilege.

00:15:54.220 --> 00:15:56.200
And that makes the Jew

00:15:56.200 --> 00:15:57.180
to be a special person.

00:15:57.280 --> 00:15:58.260
Because if you were a Jew,

00:15:59.440 --> 00:16:00.100
50 years ago,

00:16:00.160 --> 00:16:00.660
100 years ago,

00:16:00.720 --> 00:16:01.520
wherever you go,

00:16:02.360 --> 00:16:03.120
you have a hotel,

00:16:03.400 --> 00:16:04.300
you have lodging,

00:16:04.380 --> 00:16:04.600
you have this,

00:16:04.600 --> 00:16:06.700
because other Jews will always receive you.

00:16:07.220 --> 00:16:08.620
And that was a great thing that made the Jew

00:16:08.620 --> 00:16:10.240
a great people. Many things.

00:16:10.640 --> 00:16:12.460
Study Torah and so on. But one of the things that has

00:16:12.460 --> 00:16:14.500
happened, we know that wherever you go,

00:16:15.420 --> 00:16:16.620
not today, that's unfortunately

00:16:16.620 --> 00:16:18.620
not the same thing, but 50, 100 years ago,

00:16:18.680 --> 00:16:20.700
wherever you go, you know

00:16:20.700 --> 00:16:22.960
that, you know,

00:16:23.360 --> 00:16:24.000
you're going to be,

00:16:24.560 --> 00:16:26.260
somebody's going to be. I remember every

00:16:26.260 --> 00:16:27.960
story, a personal story happened to me.

00:16:29.500 --> 00:16:29.900
And

00:16:29.900 --> 00:16:32.660
it was many years ago, I was still

00:16:32.660 --> 00:16:37.780
student. I was studying at the university in Spain. Then I went for a vacation. I went

00:16:37.780 --> 00:16:47.060
to Italy. And so there they have a special residence for students. Very nice. So I went

00:16:47.060 --> 00:16:52.680
to be there. And I think I arrived at 9 before time. So my room was not reserved. I mean,

00:16:52.720 --> 00:16:58.980
it was not empty. So they said, well, you must share for tonight. You must share with

00:16:58.980 --> 00:17:04.980
somebody else. So I had no alternative. I had to share a room with someone. So I'm making

00:17:04.980 --> 00:17:09.960
the story very brief here. So I get up in the morning. I have to get up in the morning.

00:17:10.020 --> 00:17:14.080
I want to put the film in. I was there solely. And the other guy is standing there, you know,

00:17:14.480 --> 00:17:18.420
waiting, waiting, waiting. I went to where he was going to lay. The guy is not staying

00:17:18.420 --> 00:17:23.140
there. He doesn't want to move. So I said, well, you know, it's time to run. I couldn't

00:17:23.140 --> 00:17:28.840
get laid. So I said, well, I got to, you know, put the film in. I turn around. I see the

00:17:28.840 --> 00:17:29.780
guys doing the same thing.

00:17:31.280 --> 00:17:32.440
And he's Jewish too.

00:17:33.140 --> 00:17:33.580
So,

00:17:33.960 --> 00:17:36.300
you know, so what happened?

00:17:36.800 --> 00:17:37.700
The boat was shaped.

00:17:40.700 --> 00:17:42.160
It's not comfortable to pray.

00:17:42.700 --> 00:17:43.880
I mean, it's not comfortable.

00:17:44.040 --> 00:17:46.400
It's not because of being embarrassed.

00:17:46.800 --> 00:17:47.740
It's not comfortable.

00:17:48.680 --> 00:17:50.520
So, we saw the

00:17:50.520 --> 00:17:52.160
Yom Ha'Aleem and then we discovered that we're Jewish.

00:17:52.400 --> 00:17:54.580
And he showed me all around. He took me

00:17:54.580 --> 00:17:56.380
to his family

00:17:56.380 --> 00:17:58.380
was from a different city in Italy

00:17:58.380 --> 00:17:59.740
and he took me there and so on.

00:18:00.000 --> 00:18:01.940
And the whole, my whole trip

00:18:01.940 --> 00:18:03.880
was completely changed because I felt like it was

00:18:03.880 --> 00:18:05.620
like another brother.

00:18:05.780 --> 00:18:06.860
You feel it's completely different.

00:18:07.040 --> 00:18:09.360
It was already two Jews meeting each other.

00:18:09.440 --> 00:18:10.840
You meet each other, you know he's a Yehudi

00:18:10.840 --> 00:18:12.980
and that was throughout

00:18:12.980 --> 00:18:15.740
our history.

00:18:16.140 --> 00:18:16.800
Especially on this planet.

00:18:16.960 --> 00:18:19.300
For instance, we have songs that maybe

00:18:19.300 --> 00:18:20.420
originated in Morocco.

00:18:21.020 --> 00:18:21.140
Like,

00:18:21.220 --> 00:18:24.260
a song from Morocco.

00:18:24.520 --> 00:18:27.140
As we sing it. What happened?

00:18:27.140 --> 00:18:32.940
Maybe once an oréa came from Morocco to the Queens, they invited and so on, came the song and so on.

00:18:33.080 --> 00:18:34.760
And the main song that we sing, that they sing.

00:18:35.300 --> 00:18:41.960
Now there was a whole thing of interchange without discovering similar names, similar customs, similar food.

00:18:42.380 --> 00:18:49.280
Because don't forget, it's a great musbah, we should try to, you know, think about it.

00:18:49.280 --> 00:18:50.180
Yes, sir.

00:18:50.180 --> 00:18:57.680
New Yorkers, in general, I recall, the causes, you know, they're very busy.

00:18:57.940 --> 00:18:59.140
Women are too busy.

00:19:00.400 --> 00:19:01.560
They might travel.

00:19:01.760 --> 00:19:04.360
South America, Mexico, Europe, everywhere.

00:19:05.220 --> 00:19:06.020
Of course.

00:19:06.420 --> 00:19:07.980
It's too, very difficult.

00:19:07.980 --> 00:19:15.500
No, I mean, I know that it's difficult, but what I'm trying to impress is that still there are some institutions worthwhile preserving.

00:19:15.940 --> 00:19:16.780
Let's continue.

00:19:16.780 --> 00:19:18.040
They are bakaras Abraham.

00:19:19.560 --> 00:19:20.080
Abraham

00:19:20.080 --> 00:19:22.060
runs to the cows.

00:19:22.900 --> 00:19:24.720
Again, he always is running now, Abraham.

00:19:24.800 --> 00:19:26.500
After the milah, he's able to run.

00:19:27.140 --> 00:19:27.300
Alright?

00:19:28.300 --> 00:19:30.700
By kufrin bakar, he takes a young

00:19:30.700 --> 00:19:32.100
cow, ram,

00:19:32.600 --> 00:19:33.980
soft, tender,

00:19:34.940 --> 00:19:36.620
batot, and good means

00:19:36.620 --> 00:19:38.600
tender. By ten and a

00:19:38.600 --> 00:19:40.080
nahar, he gives it to one of his servants.

00:19:41.620 --> 00:19:42.200
By mahala,

00:19:42.320 --> 00:19:44.620
and the servants start cooking it.

00:19:44.620 --> 00:19:53.120
And he took butter, and milk, and that time it was considered a delicacy.

00:19:53.120 --> 00:19:58.520
And the food that he, he brought it all himself.

00:19:58.520 --> 00:20:05.120
By 10th name he put it in front of him, milk, butter, and the meat.

00:20:05.120 --> 00:20:06.120
One second.

00:20:06.120 --> 00:20:12.120
And he was strong enough to be standing up,

00:20:12.120 --> 00:20:26.740
Now, Laban al-Zafar. How come he did it? Two reasons. Reason number one, that in that time, the Isul of the Torah, that Isul was not given.

00:20:28.020 --> 00:20:34.260
There was no Isul of the Torah, the Deen of the Torah, the Basar al-Hara was prohibited later on. That's the simple and true reason.

00:20:34.260 --> 00:20:38.620
If you want to apologize, then you could say,

00:20:39.020 --> 00:20:41.100
أَكُلْتُ الْتَرَانُ تِبَشَّرْ جَدِيبَ حَلِدٍ مُؤْمِنًا

00:20:41.100 --> 00:20:42.780
Minattar is only a soup when they are cooked together.

00:20:43.000 --> 00:20:43.800
They were not cooked together.

00:20:44.800 --> 00:20:46.220
If you want to apologize further,

00:20:47.240 --> 00:20:48.820
if you eat first, drink the milk,

00:20:49.020 --> 00:20:50.120
then you are permitted to eat the meat.

00:20:50.660 --> 00:20:52.080
So maybe that's what they did.

00:20:52.160 --> 00:20:53.720
First they drank the milk, and then they ate.

00:20:53.820 --> 00:20:54.780
I don't know what happened.

00:20:55.000 --> 00:20:55.640
They were mal'akhim.

00:20:55.720 --> 00:20:56.980
I know that they were saltikim.

00:20:57.100 --> 00:20:59.780
I know that they were kosher, I presume.

00:21:00.360 --> 00:21:03.120
But whatever the reason of this,

00:21:03.120 --> 00:21:04.980
this is the, you know, I don't like to twist the

00:21:04.980 --> 00:21:06.400
piece of cake, you know, it's a simple thing.

00:21:06.780 --> 00:21:08.540
Number one, Torah was not given. Number two,

00:21:08.780 --> 00:21:10.760
according to the Torah, it's only prohibited when you cook together.

00:21:11.000 --> 00:21:12.980
Number three, maybe they had at first the milk

00:21:12.980 --> 00:21:14.520
and then the...

00:21:14.520 --> 00:21:16.540
Maybe one of the satisfying both.

00:21:16.580 --> 00:21:18.660
No, but obviously, because

00:21:18.660 --> 00:21:20.780
your head will...

00:21:20.780 --> 00:21:22.880
No, but I'm asking, you know...

00:21:22.880 --> 00:21:24.540
Some were not,

00:21:24.860 --> 00:21:27.060
they were vegetarians, they only ate the...

00:21:27.060 --> 00:21:28.480
The choice.

00:21:28.480 --> 00:21:29.920
All right.

00:21:29.920 --> 00:21:33.940
Now you're going to see

00:21:33.940 --> 00:21:34.980
the eight.

00:21:35.820 --> 00:21:36.040
Alright?

00:21:36.620 --> 00:21:37.400
After the eight,

00:21:37.520 --> 00:21:38.260
now you're going to see

00:21:38.260 --> 00:21:40.140
another aspect to the drama.

00:21:41.140 --> 00:21:42.780
A very interesting twist to the drama.

00:21:44.180 --> 00:21:46.780
They ask him,

00:21:47.500 --> 00:21:51.020
Where is Sarah your wife?

00:21:51.780 --> 00:21:52.340
Obviously,

00:21:52.820 --> 00:21:54.380
they knew that the name was Sarah.

00:21:54.940 --> 00:21:56.460
And of course by that time,

00:21:56.460 --> 00:21:58.220
Abraham Avinu knew that they were Mabachim.

00:21:59.920 --> 00:22:02.820
She is in her tent.

00:22:04.800 --> 00:22:05.560
And the Mal'at says,

00:22:06.560 --> 00:22:13.240
Sarah will have a child.

00:22:13.980 --> 00:22:15.600
And now we're going to see something very interesting.

00:22:19.320 --> 00:22:25.720
And Sarah was hearing from the door, from the entrance of her tent,

00:22:26.180 --> 00:22:29.340
and that tent was behind the other tent.

00:22:29.340 --> 00:22:32.860
It always was two tents, the tent for the men, the tent for the women,

00:22:33.200 --> 00:22:35.600
and she was in another tent, and she was listening from there.

00:22:36.440 --> 00:22:39.740
And now we're going to see something very, very significant.

00:22:40.740 --> 00:22:41.560
The Abraham de Sarah,

00:22:42.420 --> 00:22:44.440
Zekeim, Baim, Bayamim.

00:22:45.120 --> 00:22:47.720
Abraham de Sarah were already very advanced in years.

00:22:48.040 --> 00:22:49.960
Abraham Avinu was 99 years old.

00:22:51.780 --> 00:22:53.880
Hadar liyot de Sarah, orah kanashim.

00:22:54.400 --> 00:22:56.660
She no longer had a person.

00:22:57.680 --> 00:22:59.080
She was no longer a woman.

00:22:59.340 --> 00:23:02.100
In that sense, it would. Now they will become pregnant.

00:23:03.820 --> 00:23:05.120
And when she heard this,

00:23:06.360 --> 00:23:08.220
but this haqsara biker bahlimor,

00:23:08.880 --> 00:23:11.400
Sarah, she started laughing inside herself.

00:23:12.640 --> 00:23:13.180
And she said,

00:23:13.300 --> 00:23:19.880
after I became withered, like a withered plant,

00:23:21.200 --> 00:23:23.500
I'm going to have again youth?

00:23:25.000 --> 00:23:26.020
But on this I can't.

00:23:26.540 --> 00:23:28.480
And my master, I mean my husband,

00:23:28.480 --> 00:23:29.620
is old.

00:23:30.680 --> 00:23:31.860
And they were very angry.

00:23:32.300 --> 00:23:32.760
God says,

00:23:32.880 --> 00:23:33.820
why do you laugh?

00:23:34.000 --> 00:23:35.580
Why should you laugh?

00:23:36.160 --> 00:23:37.000
You're going to have a child.

00:23:37.920 --> 00:23:38.880
Let's see what happens.

00:23:41.060 --> 00:23:42.640
So now she hears the Malach

00:23:42.640 --> 00:23:45.200
saying,

00:23:45.500 --> 00:23:47.880
next year you're going to have a child.

00:23:48.920 --> 00:23:49.720
And she starts laughing.

00:23:51.220 --> 00:23:51.860
And she says,

00:23:52.020 --> 00:23:55.100
after I'm with her,

00:23:55.680 --> 00:23:56.460
I'm going to become

00:23:56.460 --> 00:23:58.240
young again.

00:23:58.480 --> 00:24:00.560
But on this again, my master is old.

00:24:03.560 --> 00:24:05.360
Rabbi Hayyaw al-Afiyah al-Shalom

00:24:05.360 --> 00:24:06.960
explains this in a beautiful explanation.

00:24:08.020 --> 00:24:08.620
He says like this.

00:24:10.340 --> 00:24:12.000
If you know, he says,

00:24:12.260 --> 00:24:13.160
Haytani Idna.

00:24:14.440 --> 00:24:16.300
Means, I already have Idna.

00:24:17.720 --> 00:24:18.960
What happened is the following.

00:24:20.360 --> 00:24:23.900
She was behind, in the tent, behind it.

00:24:25.900 --> 00:24:27.880
And she hears the angel.

00:24:28.480 --> 00:24:30.760
or a man, I don't know if he knows that he was an angel or not,

00:24:30.820 --> 00:24:34.700
saying, next year, Sarah will have a child.

00:24:35.480 --> 00:24:37.060
At that very moment,

00:24:37.760 --> 00:24:40.820
she starts flowing again.

00:24:43.060 --> 00:24:44.400
And she sees a kind of a parody.

00:24:45.600 --> 00:24:47.860
Now, after all those many years,

00:24:48.340 --> 00:24:51.240
after I became withered,

00:24:52.180 --> 00:24:53.900
I have Idna now.

00:24:55.100 --> 00:24:56.400
But you know what the parody?

00:24:56.400 --> 00:24:59.020
Adonis Aken, my husband is old.

00:24:59.200 --> 00:25:00.560
The miracle is not functioning.

00:25:00.640 --> 00:25:01.820
It's not going to function, the miracle.

00:25:03.580 --> 00:25:04.540
You know why?

00:25:04.680 --> 00:25:06.040
Because they made a miracle with me.

00:25:06.300 --> 00:25:07.080
Adonis Aken.

00:25:07.220 --> 00:25:08.120
But what kind of a miracle?

00:25:08.240 --> 00:25:10.820
I mean, it's a miracle without a purpose.

00:25:12.260 --> 00:25:14.120
Do you understand the question?

00:25:14.580 --> 00:25:16.820
Adonis Aken said, make a miracle with me.

00:25:17.240 --> 00:25:18.060
Adonis Aken.

00:25:18.220 --> 00:25:19.240
But my husband is old.

00:25:19.580 --> 00:25:20.880
He's a 99-year-old man.

00:25:23.180 --> 00:25:23.860
One second.

00:25:23.860 --> 00:25:26.480
but she was right

00:25:26.480 --> 00:25:28.660
and God is going to reprimand her

00:25:28.660 --> 00:25:29.280
he says

00:25:29.280 --> 00:25:36.920
I'm going to explain later on

00:25:36.920 --> 00:25:38.240
the next pasuk a little bit better

00:25:38.240 --> 00:25:40.560
let me go first because I want to

00:25:40.560 --> 00:25:41.700
explain one point

00:25:41.700 --> 00:25:51.420
is there anything impossible for the Lord?

00:25:51.700 --> 00:25:53.180
yes

00:25:53.180 --> 00:25:56.420
And the next day, the exact day, yes?

00:25:59.700 --> 00:26:00.360
What does it mean?

00:26:01.400 --> 00:26:03.120
Is it impossible something from the Lord?

00:26:04.260 --> 00:26:05.620
Rabbi Haim Agurati explains it.

00:26:05.800 --> 00:26:06.260
It's just like this.

00:26:08.000 --> 00:26:11.240
Actually, what Sarah was claiming is a very logical claim.

00:26:12.820 --> 00:26:15.440
This miracle makes no sense.

00:26:16.020 --> 00:26:17.040
It's a logical miracle.

00:26:17.080 --> 00:26:17.360
Why?

00:26:18.300 --> 00:26:20.240
Because if you want to make me young,

00:26:21.120 --> 00:26:22.600
so also you make my husband young.

00:26:23.180 --> 00:26:25.280
Don't make me young and my husband old.

00:26:25.940 --> 00:26:26.720
Now what do you want to make?

00:26:26.740 --> 00:26:28.280
A miracle that even if you're old,

00:26:28.920 --> 00:26:30.040
you still have children,

00:26:30.140 --> 00:26:31.940
then have us both old and having children.

00:26:33.540 --> 00:26:35.120
One young and one old.

00:26:36.800 --> 00:26:37.240
Do you understand?

00:26:37.600 --> 00:26:39.620
The miracle, it's illogical.

00:26:40.520 --> 00:26:41.040
It should be.

00:26:41.600 --> 00:26:44.420
Either Sarah becomes young

00:26:44.420 --> 00:26:45.520
and Abraham becomes young.

00:26:48.380 --> 00:26:50.620
Or, both were old

00:26:50.620 --> 00:26:51.680
and the miracle is,

00:26:51.740 --> 00:26:52.620
although both are old,

00:26:53.180 --> 00:26:53.920
Look at that chapter.

00:26:57.380 --> 00:26:59.320
Is there anything impossible of the Lord?

00:27:00.360 --> 00:27:04.640
The Lord wanted to show His power in the person into a young person.

00:27:05.860 --> 00:27:07.780
And this is the symbol of Saram.

00:27:08.520 --> 00:27:14.100
And Saram is a man who represents the old woman who becomes biologically young.

00:27:15.260 --> 00:27:16.900
This is one of the powers of the Lord.

00:27:17.980 --> 00:27:19.820
But Abraham represents another miracle.

00:27:20.500 --> 00:27:22.220
