01:03:27.000 --> 01:03:29.340
later on the description, which is shocking.

01:03:30.540 --> 01:03:30.960
May Allah,

01:03:31.360 --> 01:03:32.620
and this came out min al-shamayim,

01:03:33.620 --> 01:03:34.860
from above to below.

01:03:36.380 --> 01:03:37.840
But ya'afuqit al-alim ha'el,

01:03:37.840 --> 01:03:40.700
and all the cities started turning upside down.

01:03:41.920 --> 01:03:43.780
And the whole valley there.

01:03:47.460 --> 01:03:49.660
And all the inhabitants and all the vegetation

01:03:49.660 --> 01:03:51.700
were being swallowed up.

01:03:53.360 --> 01:03:54.500
And then, you know, but the wife,

01:03:54.620 --> 01:03:57.460
she looked behind it and she became salt.

01:03:58.040 --> 01:03:58.380
All right?

01:03:59.540 --> 01:03:59.880
Now,

01:04:01.040 --> 01:04:04.520
Now, the most shocking, interesting thing.

01:04:04.760 --> 01:04:05.940
Abraham gets up in the morning.

01:04:07.840 --> 01:04:10.280
and he looks from far away

01:04:10.280 --> 01:04:23.320
there is a smoke

01:04:23.320 --> 01:04:24.580
coming from the earth

01:04:24.580 --> 01:04:25.900
straight up

01:04:25.900 --> 01:04:29.940
like the

01:04:29.940 --> 01:04:31.480
of a

01:04:31.480 --> 01:04:33.120
furnace

01:04:33.120 --> 01:04:33.980
in which goes up

01:04:33.980 --> 01:04:34.780
straight up

01:04:34.780 --> 01:04:39.780
What goes up, straight up and falls down as the rain?

01:04:39.780 --> 01:04:43.780
An atomic explosion.

01:04:43.780 --> 01:04:46.780
An atomic explosion. Not volcanic.

01:04:46.780 --> 01:04:51.780
Because volcanic doesn't go up to the Shamari. It goes down.

01:04:51.780 --> 01:04:57.780
And there is geologists, I mean there is the most thorough studies, there is no volcanic activity at all.

01:04:57.780 --> 01:05:00.780
There was no volcanoes at all there.

01:05:00.780 --> 01:05:03.780
And it was destroyed.

01:05:03.780 --> 01:05:04.780
No.

01:05:04.780 --> 01:05:07.780
But first it rained, then it went up the hill.

01:05:07.780 --> 01:05:08.780
No, no.

01:05:08.780 --> 01:05:09.780
It's in our words.

01:05:09.780 --> 01:05:10.780
Excuse me.

01:05:10.780 --> 01:05:11.780
You're right and you're wrong.

01:05:11.780 --> 01:05:12.780
I tell you what happened.

01:05:12.780 --> 01:05:13.780
The killing comes through the rain.

01:05:13.780 --> 01:05:14.780
It doesn't come through the kibshan.

01:05:14.780 --> 01:05:15.780
But still he sees the kibshan going up.

01:05:15.780 --> 01:05:16.780
He...

01:05:16.780 --> 01:05:17.780
You see, Abraham is only to see the kibshan going up.

01:05:17.780 --> 01:05:18.780
When you are from far away, what do you see?

01:05:18.780 --> 01:05:19.780
You see the mushrooming.

01:05:19.780 --> 01:05:20.780
But you see, there are two scenes here.

01:05:20.780 --> 01:05:21.780
One is talking from the point of view of the, of the Sedamites.

01:05:21.780 --> 01:05:22.780
He's talking, says, they, they're receiving the rain.

01:05:22.780 --> 01:05:23.780
The rain is coming down.

01:05:23.780 --> 01:05:24.780
The rain is coming down.

01:05:24.780 --> 01:05:25.780
The rain is coming down.

01:05:25.780 --> 01:05:26.780
The rain is coming down.

01:05:26.780 --> 01:05:27.780
The rain is coming down.

01:05:27.780 --> 01:05:29.940
One is talking from the point of view of the

01:05:29.940 --> 01:05:31.300
Sedamites. He's talking, he says,

01:05:31.520 --> 01:05:33.640
they're receiving the rain, the rain's coming down.

01:05:34.100 --> 01:05:35.380
But from the far away from Abraham,

01:05:35.620 --> 01:05:36.780
you don't see rain coming out.

01:05:37.600 --> 01:05:39.420
You see the mushroom, mushrooming up.

01:05:39.420 --> 01:05:40.680
What the fuck can I throw at?

01:05:44.440 --> 01:05:44.840
Now,

01:05:45.420 --> 01:05:46.920
we didn't finish the whole parasha.

01:05:47.320 --> 01:05:49.220
Then we have all the things. Now let me tell you

01:05:49.220 --> 01:05:50.120
what the parasha,

01:05:50.420 --> 01:05:52.400
we have five minutes or so.

01:05:52.600 --> 01:05:53.560
Whose theory is this?

01:05:53.940 --> 01:05:56.020
Whose theory is this about the atomic bomb?

01:05:56.020 --> 01:06:04.020
I'm not saying there was an atomic bomb, but I'm saying that scientists show that this was an atomic explosion because there is high radioactivity there.

01:06:04.020 --> 01:06:12.020
As a matter of fact, they proved this, that the Dead Sea, we could have come through an atomic explosion, this kind of minerals.

01:06:12.020 --> 01:06:20.020
The Earth, there was like a big hole there. And there, in that lake, is where it used to be once the most fertile place in the world.

01:06:20.020 --> 01:06:25.020
All the kikar and all the cities were in what today is the Dead Sea.

01:06:25.020 --> 01:06:35.020
It was exploited, it was an explosion, and this enormous atomic explosion, the residue of this is the sea, the Dead Sea.

01:06:35.020 --> 01:06:46.020
And this, they say, is such a high radiation that is there, that they know that this could not have come from nature.

01:06:46.020 --> 01:06:47.900
don't understand how it came. The scientists don't know.

01:06:48.920 --> 01:06:50.040
It's one of the

01:06:50.040 --> 01:06:51.920
puzzles of

01:06:51.920 --> 01:06:53.420
history. We don't know how it came out.

01:06:53.660 --> 01:06:55.000
Now, I'm not saying that God

01:06:55.000 --> 01:06:57.080
doesn't have to throw an atomic bomb.

01:06:57.560 --> 01:06:59.820
But he produced

01:06:59.820 --> 01:07:02.100
the situation of an atomic

01:07:02.100 --> 01:07:04.040
explosion. We don't know how it came

01:07:04.040 --> 01:07:04.320
about.

01:07:06.040 --> 01:07:07.080
But the description,

01:07:08.460 --> 01:07:08.740
you know,

01:07:08.920 --> 01:07:11.400
that you see from far away,

01:07:11.400 --> 01:07:12.180
and him fear.

01:07:13.980 --> 01:07:14.640
Him fear.

01:07:14.640 --> 01:07:16.880
It's an atomic fallout.

01:07:18.460 --> 01:07:18.720
You know?

01:07:19.340 --> 01:07:20.880
This is an outstanding thing.

01:07:21.580 --> 01:07:21.900
Now...

01:07:21.900 --> 01:07:23.640
The area looks like...

01:07:23.640 --> 01:07:27.300
The area looks like somebody emptied out the ocean.

01:07:28.200 --> 01:07:29.680
And they're driving through the ocean.

01:07:30.300 --> 01:07:32.420
I mean, you see all the rivers that you've been in.

01:07:32.480 --> 01:07:35.020
Yeah, but they know that this didn't come out

01:07:35.020 --> 01:07:36.680
through a geological situation that was there.

01:07:36.800 --> 01:07:38.540
It's like an anomaly.

01:07:38.900 --> 01:07:40.400
In other words, if there would have been, for instance,

01:07:40.480 --> 01:07:42.180
volcanoes around it, or something like this,

01:07:42.180 --> 01:07:43.060
but they don't.

01:07:43.060 --> 01:07:45.060
That's right. The whole thing, but

01:07:45.060 --> 01:07:46.620
somebody emptied out the ocean.

01:07:48.220 --> 01:07:49.260
But that ocean is

01:07:49.260 --> 01:07:50.820
full of Weizmann,

01:07:51.300 --> 01:07:53.000
who was the first president of Israel.

01:07:53.320 --> 01:07:55.280
He was a very distinguished chemist at the

01:07:55.280 --> 01:07:56.800
same time. You know, he was a good chemist.

01:07:57.180 --> 01:07:58.180
He won a prize.

01:07:59.740 --> 01:08:01.000
I mean, I don't know much about

01:08:01.000 --> 01:08:03.280
chemistry, but he was supposed to have been a distinguished

01:08:03.280 --> 01:08:05.300
chemist. And one of the

01:08:05.300 --> 01:08:07.220
reasons why he wanted, in the partition, wanted to

01:08:07.220 --> 01:08:09.240
have the Dead Sea for us is because he knew

01:08:09.240 --> 01:08:10.740
that the Dead Sea is one of the richest

01:08:10.740 --> 01:08:13.120
places for minerals in the whole world.

01:08:13.480 --> 01:08:15.020
But there's other things, I don't know what

01:08:15.020 --> 01:08:16.160
there is there, you know.

01:08:16.380 --> 01:08:19.020
So let me make

01:08:19.020 --> 01:08:20.360
a very short summary

01:08:20.360 --> 01:08:21.820
of this Takvara.

01:08:21.820 --> 01:08:22.460
Alright?

01:08:24.300 --> 01:08:25.480
Summary goes as follows.

01:08:26.360 --> 01:08:27.940
Abraham Avinu, old man,

01:08:28.980 --> 01:08:29.740
Shara'a Menu,

01:08:30.760 --> 01:08:31.480
God tell him

01:08:31.480 --> 01:08:33.920
make Milah,

01:08:35.600 --> 01:08:36.260
Kehomayom,

01:08:36.420 --> 01:08:37.460
his heart is tired,

01:08:37.580 --> 01:08:39.360
all of a sudden he sees a vision,

01:08:39.360 --> 01:08:44.740
He becomes like a young man, running, jumping, doing things.

01:08:45.960 --> 01:08:49.020
Sarah becomes a young woman.

01:08:50.380 --> 01:08:52.720
Eventually, they have a child named Ishaq.

01:08:55.080 --> 01:09:02.880
Meanwhile, let's contrast Abraham and his first child, his wife, Ishaq,

01:09:03.560 --> 01:09:06.700
and his good friend, his partner, Lot.

01:09:06.700 --> 01:09:09.060
and the contrast already

01:09:09.060 --> 01:09:11.520
make us realize the greatness of Abraham

01:09:11.520 --> 01:09:12.480
and the dangers

01:09:12.480 --> 01:09:15.880
involved in being in a society

01:09:15.880 --> 01:09:16.480
like Sodom

01:09:16.480 --> 01:09:18.280
because we know what happened to Lot

01:09:18.280 --> 01:09:21.380
on the one hand, Lot wanted to do good

01:09:21.380 --> 01:09:23.160
but even in the moment of goodness

01:09:23.160 --> 01:09:24.660
he was doing perverted things

01:09:24.660 --> 01:09:26.620
and just compare the first children

01:09:26.620 --> 01:09:29.880
Isaac with Moab and Ammon

01:09:29.880 --> 01:09:31.900
the way Abraham and Sarah

01:09:31.900 --> 01:09:33.020
they conceived a child

01:09:33.020 --> 01:09:34.080
and the way Lot

01:09:34.080 --> 01:09:36.380
and his two daughters

01:09:36.380 --> 01:09:41.380
The Torah does it in a very subtle way, for anybody who is intelligent, to make a comparison.

01:09:41.380 --> 01:09:49.380
And still, Abraham was not a czar, because he prayed for Sodom and Gomorrah.

01:09:49.380 --> 01:09:57.380
Abraham was a man full of compassion, because he was arguing on behalf of Sodom and Gomorrah.

01:09:57.380 --> 01:10:00.380
God give him a chance, another chance, another chance, another chance.

01:10:00.380 --> 01:10:05.380
You see, until finally they realized there is not even a minyan.

01:10:05.380 --> 01:10:06.340
There is no minyan.

01:10:07.340 --> 01:10:07.620
So,

01:10:08.040 --> 01:10:09.800
there is no more hope.

01:10:12.120 --> 01:10:12.600
Now,

01:10:13.600 --> 01:10:14.260
an explosion,

01:10:14.540 --> 01:10:15.120
Salam al-Mahamara

01:10:15.120 --> 01:10:15.780
disappeared.

01:10:16.940 --> 01:10:17.820
Two more events.

01:10:19.380 --> 01:10:20.100
And with these

01:10:20.100 --> 01:10:20.920
two more events,

01:10:21.180 --> 01:10:21.960
we finish the parashah.

01:10:22.820 --> 01:10:23.660
One event,

01:10:24.360 --> 01:10:25.260
after the Salam al-Mahamara

01:10:25.260 --> 01:10:25.800
and so on,

01:10:25.840 --> 01:10:26.580
the story and so on,

01:10:26.660 --> 01:10:28.460
the difference between

01:10:28.460 --> 01:10:29.300
the Lord and Abraham,

01:10:29.680 --> 01:10:29.860
you know,

01:10:30.160 --> 01:10:30.960
we started both of them

01:10:30.960 --> 01:10:31.560
the same way.

01:10:32.160 --> 01:10:32.720
The Lord would have been

01:10:32.720 --> 01:10:33.000
a great,

01:10:33.060 --> 01:10:33.600
maybe one day

01:10:33.600 --> 01:10:34.960
the Lord would have been

01:10:34.960 --> 01:10:35.960
great men.

01:10:35.960 --> 01:10:36.780
You don't know.

01:10:36.780 --> 01:10:37.780
But, change.

01:10:37.780 --> 01:10:38.780
Change of orientation.

01:10:38.780 --> 01:10:39.780
After this, Abraham and Sarah are passing.

01:10:39.780 --> 01:10:44.780
Abimelech sees Sarah and he wants to kidnap her, to take her as his wife.

01:10:44.780 --> 01:11:03.620
Proof of the beauty of Sarah on the one hand and the miracles that happened there.

01:11:03.620 --> 01:11:07.800
But then comes the last trial of Abraham.

01:11:08.660 --> 01:11:10.940
God tells him, I changed my mind.

01:11:11.700 --> 01:11:12.840
I changed my mind, God says.

01:11:13.820 --> 01:11:15.900
It's hard, I don't know, it's hard not to be your son.

01:11:16.880 --> 01:11:20.340
The children, it's hard, but the promise that they say, I've changed all my mind about my promise.

01:11:20.460 --> 01:11:21.860
You know what I want you to do with your son?

01:11:22.840 --> 01:11:24.940
Take him to Hala Moriah and kill him there.

01:11:26.940 --> 01:11:28.240
Now Abraham is 100 years old.

01:11:28.240 --> 01:11:32.760
More than 100, 120, 199, plus 37, plus 120.

01:11:32.760 --> 01:11:35.160
136.

01:11:35.880 --> 01:11:36.520
136.

01:11:38.080 --> 01:11:38.740
That says,

01:11:39.160 --> 01:11:41.060
Abraham, sorry,

01:11:42.020 --> 01:11:43.680
you know, I promise you,

01:11:45.620 --> 01:11:47.400
130, whatever it is.

01:11:47.480 --> 01:11:49.120
It was no longer

01:11:49.120 --> 01:11:50.180
a young man.

01:11:50.180 --> 01:11:52.140
His heart was

01:11:52.140 --> 01:11:53.600
at the time 37 years old.

01:11:53.820 --> 01:11:55.400
Abraham was 99.

01:11:56.100 --> 01:11:57.260
So he was 136.

01:11:58.240 --> 01:11:59.140
136 years old.

01:11:59.140 --> 01:12:07.680
So, 136 years old, God says to Abraham, listen, change my mind.

01:12:08.160 --> 01:12:12.460
I promise you that keep his heart, that his heart will do it.

01:12:13.160 --> 01:12:15.300
I'm going to give you a child to your children.

01:12:16.280 --> 01:12:17.140
Change my mind.

01:12:17.740 --> 01:12:18.740
You know what I would like you to do?

01:12:19.780 --> 01:12:21.900
Take this child, his heart.

01:12:23.040 --> 01:12:24.200
37 years old.

01:12:25.200 --> 01:12:28.140
This young man, you know, this young man, take him.

01:12:28.140 --> 01:12:29.860
take him to Al-Muriyah

01:12:29.860 --> 01:12:32.180
and just do one thing, just kill him there

01:12:32.180 --> 01:12:33.580
I know Shami Allah

01:12:33.580 --> 01:12:38.080
now

01:12:38.080 --> 01:12:39.840
you have to

01:12:39.840 --> 01:12:41.980
put yourself in the place of Abraham

01:12:41.980 --> 01:12:44.520
God made him

01:12:44.520 --> 01:12:46.300
live at the age of 75

01:12:46.300 --> 01:12:47.060
years old

01:12:47.060 --> 01:12:50.520
from Haran all the way

01:12:50.520 --> 01:12:52.220
to Israel, all the trials

01:12:52.220 --> 01:12:53.920
tribulations, everything that happened

01:12:53.920 --> 01:12:54.740
everything this

01:12:54.740 --> 01:12:57.100
and the promise, God promised him

01:12:57.100 --> 01:13:04.100
His heart is going to be your son and he is going to become his children, they are going to take possession of this land.

01:13:04.100 --> 01:13:07.100
You know what I want you to do? I want you to kill them.

01:13:07.100 --> 01:13:13.100
They think of Abraham, what kind of a God is he?

01:13:13.100 --> 01:13:16.100
God all of a sudden wants my child to be killed, a human being to be killed.

01:13:16.100 --> 01:13:24.100
But Abraham Avinu, Abraham Avinu does not even protest, does not even argue.

01:13:24.100 --> 01:13:29.100
He takes his pot, puts him to the mountain, you know,

01:13:29.100 --> 01:13:35.100
he ties him up, he takes the maqal, he's ready to do it.

01:13:35.100 --> 01:13:37.100
He goes into the desert.

01:13:37.100 --> 01:13:39.100
And the Pasuhr says,

01:13:45.100 --> 01:13:48.100
Now I know that you really are a Re'rohim.

01:13:48.100 --> 01:13:51.100
What does it mean, now I know?

01:13:51.100 --> 01:13:58.100
It's one of the most difficult things. God doesn't know. I mean, God doesn't know that Abraham is in Jiray, you know what I mean?

01:13:58.100 --> 01:14:01.100
He needs to have this kind of test?

01:14:01.100 --> 01:14:04.100
Al-Tahak?

01:14:04.100 --> 01:14:13.100
I love the Shalom that Rabbi Moshe Hefes, he says, the real meaning of Ar-Taya Da'atih.

01:14:13.100 --> 01:14:19.100
It's so simple, you know. I read this a thousand times, you know, we read it every day in the morning.

01:14:19.100 --> 01:14:24.100
I never realized I'm the library of the Rabi Moshe Heres.

01:14:24.100 --> 01:14:29.100
If you pay attention, what is the meaning of the word, now I know.

01:14:29.100 --> 01:14:36.100
But in Hebrew, it's like a past tense.

01:14:36.100 --> 01:14:39.100
It says, now I knew.

01:14:39.100 --> 01:14:43.100
He said,

01:14:43.100 --> 01:14:46.100
What is it?

01:14:46.100 --> 01:14:48.940
He says, I know it all the time.

01:14:49.300 --> 01:14:52.720
I know it all the time that you could get me out of this.

01:14:52.760 --> 01:14:54.140
That means that now I know.

01:14:54.360 --> 01:14:55.800
Like we translate wrongly in English.

01:14:56.320 --> 01:14:58.340
I know it all the time.

01:15:00.880 --> 01:15:02.520
It's not to say, it's to show the world.

01:15:02.620 --> 01:15:03.960
It's not that God doesn't know.

01:15:04.760 --> 01:15:05.880
It's to show, no.

01:15:06.060 --> 01:15:07.260
It's not a test in the sense.

01:15:07.700 --> 01:15:08.840
It's to show the world

01:15:08.840 --> 01:15:12.700
who Abraham is.

01:15:14.240 --> 01:15:15.340
Abraham could have said to God,

01:15:15.340 --> 01:15:16.880
listen, I'm sorry, I'm not going to listen to you.

01:15:17.200 --> 01:15:19.360
Because you promised me, and I have it

01:15:19.360 --> 01:15:21.540
black and white. You stay, keep

01:15:21.540 --> 01:15:22.860
his house, and call him a Hazara.

01:15:23.880 --> 01:15:25.180
And you told me this, and you told me

01:15:25.180 --> 01:15:27.160
this is going to be an event. So why are you going to tell me

01:15:27.160 --> 01:15:27.800
to kill my son?

01:15:29.280 --> 01:15:32.620
How could you play with that?

01:15:33.080 --> 01:15:34.340
How could you tell me to kill somebody?

01:15:36.280 --> 01:15:36.840
But Abraham

01:15:36.840 --> 01:15:39.480
didn't do it. Didn't protest.

01:15:39.880 --> 01:15:40.580
Didn't argue.

01:15:42.720 --> 01:15:43.320
And that's

01:15:43.320 --> 01:15:45.180
why it says in the Nabi, Abraham

01:15:45.180 --> 01:15:48.620
Oh Habib, Abraham is the one who loves me.

01:15:49.240 --> 01:15:51.020
What does it mean to love according to Jewish law?

01:15:52.120 --> 01:15:56.500
It means to accept someone unconditionally.

01:15:58.220 --> 01:16:00.440
You should love God.

01:16:06.360 --> 01:16:06.800
Unconditionally.

01:16:07.960 --> 01:16:09.820
You believe that it's not possible, it is possible.

01:16:09.940 --> 01:16:10.820
Abraham Oh Habib.

01:16:12.320 --> 01:16:14.140
And God knew it all the time.

01:16:14.140 --> 01:16:18.160
What is happening now

01:16:18.160 --> 01:16:19.780
I knew it all the time

01:16:19.780 --> 01:16:22.280
I'm affirming what I knew

01:16:22.280 --> 01:16:23.360
Exactly

01:16:23.360 --> 01:16:24.720
I'm affirming

01:16:24.720 --> 01:16:28.060
Now came to pass what I knew

01:16:28.060 --> 01:16:29.100
Already previously

01:16:29.100 --> 01:16:31.700
Excuse me Rabbi

01:16:31.700 --> 01:16:33.800
Can we assume Abraham knew

01:16:33.800 --> 01:16:35.220
That God is testing him

01:16:35.220 --> 01:16:38.600
He knew he was testing him

01:16:38.600 --> 01:16:39.840
And he wasn't taking any chances

01:16:39.840 --> 01:16:41.000
He knew he was testing him

01:16:41.000 --> 01:16:42.680
As a matter of fact

01:16:42.680 --> 01:16:43.480
the haqqamim

01:16:43.480 --> 01:16:44.140
they say that already

01:16:44.140 --> 01:16:45.140
he can start cutting

01:16:45.140 --> 01:16:46.800
but even at that point

01:16:46.800 --> 01:16:47.220
he didn't

01:16:47.220 --> 01:16:47.800
no

01:16:47.800 --> 01:16:49.020
because he promised

01:16:49.020 --> 01:16:49.620
him he was going to

01:16:49.620 --> 01:16:50.300
have to do that

01:16:50.300 --> 01:16:50.540
no

01:16:50.540 --> 01:16:53.480
but Allah knows

01:16:53.480 --> 01:16:54.280
the heart of people

01:16:54.280 --> 01:16:55.460
certainly

01:16:55.460 --> 01:16:56.080
please haqqam

01:16:56.080 --> 01:16:57.840
in this sense

01:16:57.840 --> 01:16:58.180
there is another

01:16:58.180 --> 01:16:58.720
interpretation

01:16:58.720 --> 01:16:59.460
that I think

01:16:59.460 --> 01:16:59.960
would fit

01:16:59.960 --> 01:17:01.360
our reasoning

01:17:01.360 --> 01:17:02.520
if we look at

01:17:02.520 --> 01:17:03.000
the word nisa

01:17:03.000 --> 01:17:04.400
nisa comes from

01:17:04.400 --> 01:17:05.120
the word nis

01:17:05.120 --> 01:17:06.180
the harim nis

01:17:06.180 --> 01:17:07.060
means to raise

01:17:07.060 --> 01:17:07.420
something

01:17:07.420 --> 01:17:08.340
to raise a flag

01:17:08.340 --> 01:17:10.240
to put a pot

01:17:10.240 --> 01:17:11.700
so God

01:17:11.700 --> 01:17:12.440
did not want

01:17:12.440 --> 01:17:13.040
to test Abraham.

01:17:13.740 --> 01:17:14.580
He's not testing him

01:17:14.580 --> 01:17:15.260
because God knows

01:17:15.260 --> 01:17:15.740
and he doesn't have

01:17:15.740 --> 01:17:16.200
to test Abraham.

01:17:16.400 --> 01:17:17.720
He knows what he's got.

01:17:18.340 --> 01:17:19.320
The person knows his son.

01:17:19.440 --> 01:17:19.760
He knows him.

01:17:20.520 --> 01:17:20.940
But he wanted

01:17:20.940 --> 01:17:25.320
to show him to the world

01:17:25.320 --> 01:17:26.240
look what I have.

01:17:26.320 --> 01:17:27.140
Look what I chose.

01:17:27.560 --> 01:17:28.120
Look at the person

01:17:28.120 --> 01:17:28.760
that I chose.

01:17:29.100 --> 01:17:29.500
So the way

01:17:29.500 --> 01:17:30.240
does not come more

01:17:30.240 --> 01:17:30.680
of a test

01:17:30.680 --> 01:17:33.060
but to raise a flag

01:17:33.060 --> 01:17:34.780
to demonstrate

01:17:34.780 --> 01:17:35.200
to show him

01:17:35.200 --> 01:17:36.280
what's the world

01:17:36.280 --> 01:17:37.260
what kind of person

01:17:37.260 --> 01:17:37.620
I have.

01:17:37.720 --> 01:17:38.200
Very nice.

01:17:38.520 --> 01:17:39.560
How would you consider

01:17:39.560 --> 01:17:41.160
a 37 year old man

01:17:41.160 --> 01:17:42.060
going and listening

01:17:42.060 --> 01:17:43.480
to his father, ready to go.

01:17:43.680 --> 01:17:44.500
He had respect there.

01:17:46.720 --> 01:17:48.020
Mickey, Mickey,

01:17:48.120 --> 01:17:50.320
you know what I said. I want to repeat what I said.

01:17:50.400 --> 01:17:51.440
When I was in

01:17:51.440 --> 01:17:53.860
the church in

01:17:53.860 --> 01:17:56.200
Magin David, I said a few words for Rosh Hashanah.

01:17:56.320 --> 01:17:57.180
I was invited to say a few words.

01:17:57.660 --> 01:18:00.160
And I was invited, I think I wasn't prepared at all.

01:18:00.460 --> 01:18:02.180
So I mean, I was in despair

01:18:02.180 --> 01:18:02.620
at the moment.

01:18:03.460 --> 01:18:05.820
And then I said,

01:18:05.920 --> 01:18:08.000
I discussed some ideas. And one of the points

01:18:08.000 --> 01:18:09.720
I discussed is why

01:18:09.720 --> 01:18:11.300
wait a second,

01:18:11.300 --> 01:18:12.060
or this is

01:18:12.060 --> 01:18:12.700
makes me up.

01:18:13.020 --> 01:18:13.640
Makes me up.

01:18:14.040 --> 01:18:14.820
I love this thing.

01:18:17.740 --> 01:18:18.140
Why?

01:18:19.080 --> 01:18:20.120
I took the whole idea

01:18:20.120 --> 01:18:20.720
of the Akedah

01:18:20.720 --> 01:18:21.980
and I put it

01:18:21.980 --> 01:18:22.760
onto a simple thing.

01:18:23.400 --> 01:18:24.040
We always

01:18:24.040 --> 01:18:26.080
realize that

01:18:26.080 --> 01:18:26.840
when we were children

01:18:26.840 --> 01:18:28.520
we were willing

01:18:28.520 --> 01:18:29.540
to obey our parents.

01:18:31.460 --> 01:18:32.320
We were willing

01:18:32.320 --> 01:18:33.540
to obey our parents.

01:18:33.580 --> 01:18:34.420
To a certain degree.

01:18:34.760 --> 01:18:35.160
But no.

01:18:35.240 --> 01:18:36.480
We say that we obey them.

01:18:36.620 --> 01:18:37.760
We obey them all the way.

01:18:39.200 --> 01:18:40.080
But our children

01:18:40.080 --> 01:18:42.600
refused to obey us.

01:18:42.760 --> 01:18:44.360
They refused to listen to us.

01:18:45.280 --> 01:18:46.860
So what is going on? Why is it like this?

01:18:47.580 --> 01:18:48.660
So the answer to this is

01:18:48.660 --> 01:18:50.360
in the parashah of the haqqiyat of Ishaq.

01:18:52.140 --> 01:18:52.580
Ishaq

01:18:52.580 --> 01:18:53.700
was willing to

01:18:53.700 --> 01:18:56.760
let himself be killed by Abraham Avinu.

01:18:58.920 --> 01:19:00.620
Why Abraham Avinu had this influence?

01:19:01.380 --> 01:19:02.400
Because before

01:19:02.400 --> 01:19:04.220
Abraham Avinu tells Ishaq

01:19:04.220 --> 01:19:06.480
to give himself

01:19:06.480 --> 01:19:08.220
for God, to submit,

01:19:08.220 --> 01:19:09.400
Abraham,

01:19:09.660 --> 01:19:12.120
first Abraham

01:19:12.120 --> 01:19:13.160
builds an altar.

01:19:14.560 --> 01:19:15.460
Our parents,

01:19:16.660 --> 01:19:18.540
and Abraham was the first of our parents,

01:19:18.760 --> 01:19:20.020
he first built an altar.

01:19:20.420 --> 01:19:21.980
Once the father builds an altar,

01:19:22.740 --> 01:19:24.560
the son is willing to

01:19:24.560 --> 01:19:26.640
stretch his neck and say,

01:19:26.880 --> 01:19:28.360
Father, go ahead and do it.

01:19:28.420 --> 01:19:29.220
Do what you have to do.

01:19:29.220 --> 01:19:31.640
So did he ask where is the...

01:19:31.640 --> 01:19:33.340
Yes, but he asked.

01:19:33.600 --> 01:19:33.980
And so he said,

01:19:34.020 --> 01:19:36.260
he wouldn't leave the altar, he put it back.

01:19:36.260 --> 01:19:38.380
our parents built an altar

01:19:38.380 --> 01:19:39.980
and because our parents built an altar

01:19:39.980 --> 01:19:41.580
we were willing to submit.

01:19:42.840 --> 01:19:44.300
Our children they don't submit

01:19:44.300 --> 01:19:46.280
because we do not

01:19:46.280 --> 01:19:47.300
build altars.

01:19:48.360 --> 01:19:50.180
As soon as we build a Mizbeah

01:19:50.180 --> 01:19:52.580
in our homes, you're going to see

01:19:52.580 --> 01:19:54.180
just like we listen to our parents

01:19:54.180 --> 01:19:56.220
our children

01:19:56.220 --> 01:19:58.400
will listen to us. This is the Abraham

01:19:58.400 --> 01:20:00.020
even Abraham is a Mizbeah.

01:20:00.840 --> 01:20:02.220
And then we are according to the Quran.

01:20:06.260 --> 01:20:08.160
Blame the parents.

01:20:08.740 --> 01:20:09.200
I beg your pardon?

01:20:09.500 --> 01:20:10.320
Blame the parents.

01:20:10.620 --> 01:20:10.960
Of course.

01:20:11.120 --> 01:20:11.600
Of course.

01:20:12.060 --> 01:20:13.780
And I tell you, you know why we didn't go back?

01:20:13.820 --> 01:20:14.780
Not because we were so good.

01:20:14.900 --> 01:20:16.080
Because our parents were good.

01:20:17.440 --> 01:20:19.420
Let us say that we were not the good ones.

01:20:20.540 --> 01:20:21.960
Our parents were the good ones.

01:20:22.560 --> 01:20:23.640
Leave a little credit for it.

01:20:23.720 --> 01:20:24.120
Just a little bit.

01:20:24.440 --> 01:20:24.680
No.

01:20:25.160 --> 01:20:25.680
That's fine.

01:20:27.320 --> 01:20:29.800
But you know, our parents, they do what they do.

01:20:30.160 --> 01:20:31.080
They were scared too.

01:20:31.720 --> 01:20:33.160
But not only scared.

01:20:33.260 --> 01:20:34.500
But we cannot scare our children.

01:20:34.500 --> 01:20:35.620
because it's not a question of just,

01:20:35.820 --> 01:20:38.120
our parents built a Mizbeah.

01:20:38.280 --> 01:20:39.440
We knew that our parents

01:20:39.440 --> 01:20:40.280
meant something.

01:20:43.280 --> 01:20:45.660
A few thoughts came to my mind

01:20:45.660 --> 01:20:46.740
and I'd like to say them

01:20:46.740 --> 01:20:48.940
because I think you'll find them

01:20:48.940 --> 01:20:49.420
a little interesting.

01:20:50.540 --> 01:20:52.420
The Torah means

01:20:52.420 --> 01:20:55.040
to teach a way of life.

01:20:55.360 --> 01:20:55.760
The Horot,

01:20:56.760 --> 01:20:59.260
it doesn't come to give us only stories,

01:20:59.760 --> 01:21:01.380
but to teach us certain things

01:21:01.380 --> 01:21:03.620
that will improve our thinking,

01:21:03.620 --> 01:21:04.500
improve our life

01:21:04.500 --> 01:21:05.880
and make us

01:21:05.880 --> 01:21:06.660
better people

01:21:06.660 --> 01:21:07.580
to appreciate life

01:21:07.580 --> 01:21:08.840
and know how to live.

01:21:10.100 --> 01:21:10.960
One of the things

01:21:10.960 --> 01:21:11.880
the Rabbi just mentioned

01:21:11.880 --> 01:21:12.660
the three things

01:21:12.660 --> 01:21:13.780
the three highlights

01:21:13.780 --> 01:21:14.500
of this pirashat

01:21:14.500 --> 01:21:15.960
one of them is

01:21:15.960 --> 01:21:18.080
that a man

01:21:18.080 --> 01:21:19.880
happens to be

01:21:19.880 --> 01:21:20.900
a part of his environment.

01:21:22.600 --> 01:21:23.220
We see Lord

01:21:23.220 --> 01:21:24.300
who was a pure

01:21:24.300 --> 01:21:25.100
and good man

01:21:25.100 --> 01:21:25.860
when he was under

01:21:25.860 --> 01:21:26.600
the influence of Abraham

01:21:26.600 --> 01:21:27.980
as soon as he went

01:21:27.980 --> 01:21:29.020
with Tzedon

01:21:29.020 --> 01:21:30.560
already he became

01:21:30.560 --> 01:21:31.400
a different man.

01:21:31.960 --> 01:21:32.520
That's why

01:21:32.520 --> 01:21:34.580
we have to be very careful

01:21:34.580 --> 01:21:37.020
that we always be,

01:21:37.260 --> 01:21:39.140
we always mix, and we always remain

01:21:39.140 --> 01:21:41.240
with our own kind. We always make sure

01:21:41.240 --> 01:21:43.400
that our children remain under their own people.

01:21:44.180 --> 01:21:45.400
The second thing that we

01:21:45.400 --> 01:21:46.420
learn from it,

01:21:48.420 --> 01:21:55.360
the second thing that we learn

01:21:55.360 --> 01:21:57.240
from it, we look at Abraham and Abinu

01:21:57.240 --> 01:21:59.360
and we point out, why did God choose

01:21:59.360 --> 01:22:00.660
Abraham rather than choose

01:22:00.660 --> 01:22:02.900
Noah

01:22:02.900 --> 01:22:03.840
Noah Hayari

01:22:03.840 --> 01:22:04.500
Sadiq Kameen

01:22:04.500 --> 01:22:05.200
he was also

01:22:05.200 --> 01:22:05.780
a righteous man

01:22:05.780 --> 01:22:07.660
why did he have to wait

01:22:07.660 --> 01:22:08.620
till Abraham came along

01:22:08.620 --> 01:22:09.780
why wasn't he satisfied

01:22:09.780 --> 01:22:10.540
with Noah

01:22:10.540 --> 01:22:11.460
let him be the

01:22:11.460 --> 01:22:12.160
first Jew

01:22:12.160 --> 01:22:13.120
and then

01:22:13.120 --> 01:22:13.760
Abraham would be

01:22:13.760 --> 01:22:14.320
his descendant

01:22:14.320 --> 01:22:15.280
but

01:22:15.280 --> 01:22:16.800
there's one big difference

01:22:16.800 --> 01:22:17.340
between Abraham

01:22:17.340 --> 01:22:18.000
and Noah

01:22:18.000 --> 01:22:19.740
and if we pay attention

01:22:19.740 --> 01:22:20.180
to this parasha

01:22:20.180 --> 01:22:21.700
I think this is the essence

01:22:21.700 --> 01:22:22.880
of our Judaism

01:22:22.880 --> 01:22:23.580
it's the essence

01:22:23.580 --> 01:22:24.620
of why we are

01:22:24.620 --> 01:22:25.420
Jewish people

01:22:25.420 --> 01:22:26.100
why we're chosen

01:22:26.100 --> 01:22:27.760
to be Jewish people

01:22:27.760 --> 01:22:29.160
when God came

01:22:29.160 --> 01:22:29.680
and told Noah

01:22:29.680 --> 01:22:32.680
that I'm going to bring a flood,

01:22:32.800 --> 01:22:33.940
that I'm going to destroy the world.

01:22:34.940 --> 01:22:36.000
Noah was already satisfied

01:22:36.000 --> 01:22:37.820
to go into the boat.

01:22:37.820 --> 01:22:38.520
Just a minute.

01:22:45.020 --> 01:22:46.680
Noah was ready to go into the boat

01:22:46.680 --> 01:22:48.040
and save his own skin.

01:22:48.700 --> 01:22:49.640
While Abraham Avinu,

01:22:50.100 --> 01:22:52.400
he was not only satisfied with his own self,

01:22:52.840 --> 01:22:54.820
he was even concerned and worried about...

01:22:59.680 --> 01:23:29.660
Thank you.

01:23:29.680 --> 01:23:59.660
Thank you.

01:23:59.680 --> 01:24:29.660
Thank you.

01:24:29.680 --> 01:24:59.660
Thank you.

01:24:59.680 --> 01:25:29.660
Thank you.

01:25:29.680 --> 01:25:59.660
Thank you.

01:25:59.680 --> 01:26:29.660
Thank you.

01:26:29.680 --> 01:26:59.660
Thank you.

01:26:59.680 --> 01:27:29.660
Thank you.

01:27:29.680 --> 01:27:59.660
Thank you.

01:27:59.680 --> 01:28:29.660
Thank you.

01:28:29.680 --> 01:28:59.660
Thank you.

01:28:59.680 --> 01:29:29.660
Thank you.

01:29:29.680 --> 01:29:59.660
Thank you.

01:29:59.680 --> 01:30:29.660
Thank you.

